You got some of that right and I think you understood what the original issue with the code was. However the statement about "the last arg is not really used" is a bit off. Take e.g. the original linked tlpi example. With a properly null terminated sun_path passed in the sockaddr_un the len can be anything between 15 and 108 in the client sendto() call. Lenghts less than 15 give an error in sendto. The len is clearly used in kernel code.

